msgid "banesword"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Caror.cfg:57
msgid "sand storm"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Caror.cfg:70
msgid "shadow stifle"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Familiar, race=undead
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Familiar.cfg:18
msgid "Powerful magic users sometimes have familiars, creatures which have had a spirit or minor demon drawn into them. A familiar may act as a spy or messenger for its master."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Fighter, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Fighter.cfg:4
msgid "Wesfolk Fighter"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Fighter, race=human
#. Ці бійці є невід'ємними представниками нечисельної людської частини армії західняків. Хоч і усі загарбники в ранньому віці присягають Темряві на вічну службу та проводять огидний ритуал, велика частина з них все ж не має природнього дару до магії, тому в бою їм доводиться покладатися лише на спритність та вірну mace-spiked
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Fighter.cfg:17
msgid "These soldiers are essential representatives of the sparse alive part of the invader's army. Although almost all of Wesfolk swear eternal service to the Darkness at an early age and perform their hideous rituals, most of them still have no natural gift for magic, so in battle they have to rely only on agility and a trusty mace with spikes."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Fighter.cfg:22
msgid "mace-spiked"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Lenvan, race=undead
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Lenvan.cfg:4
msgid "Lich-Lord of Trickery"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=arcane
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Lenvan.cfg:29
msgid "touch"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=cold
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Lenvan.cfg:42
msgid "chill tempest"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=fire
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Lenvan.cfg:54
msgid "ruby of fire"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Marauder, race=human, gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Marauder.cfg:4
msgid "Wesfolk Marauder"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Marauder, race=human, gender=male,female
#. Взяти до рук велику сіть було достатньо логічним рішенням для деяких з Footpads — все ж західнякам постійно потрібні живі жертвоприношення, для здійснення своїх темних ритуалів. Хоч і за важких умов можна використати когось зі своїх, все ж краще захопити чужинця, чиї жахливі крики звучатимуть гарною музикою для всіх присутніх поклонників темряви.
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Marauder.cfg:20
msgid "Capturing a large net was a logical enough decision for some of the Footpads - after all, Wesfolk always need live sacrifices to perform their dark rituals. Although it is possible to use one of their own, it's still better to capture a stranger whose horrific screams will sound like good music to all the worshippers of Darkness present."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Marauder.cfg:25
msgid "morning star"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Marauder.cfg:34
msgid "net"
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Marauder.cfg:70
msgid "female^Marauder"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Necroprincess, gender=female, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Princess_Necro.cfg:8
msgid "Princess of Battle"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Necroprincess, gender=female, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Princess_Necro.cfg:26
msgid ""
"Although not actually of royal blood, Wesfolk Princesses play an important role in their wicked society as loyal servants of the Lich-Lords, leading their armies and fulfilling their every demand.\n"
"Princesses are not born, but become them after many years of exhausting training, dark rituals and difficult trials, for which they are highly respected by other Wesfolk people and even some of the powerful undead."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Princess_Necro.cfg:32
msgid "staff of rage"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=cold
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Princess_Necro.cfg:45
msgid "chill wave"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=pseudoghoul, race=undead
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Pseudoghoul.cfg:4
msgid "Pseudoghoul"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=pseudoghoul, race=undead
#. Чи то через нестачу знань, чи то спеціально, темні адепти часту зупиняють процес перетворення людини на гуля на проміжному етапі, коли людина ще є живою, відчуває все, що з нею відбувається, проте вже припиняє бути собою, хоч і не сильно нагадує роздуте огидне чудовисько. Таких істот називають псевдогулями — вони виглядають як щось схоже до ходячого трупа, проте з їхнього мутованого рота невеликими потоками струїться зелена кислота, якою вони можуть плюватися, щоб отруїти ворогів некроманта, який пішов на такий огидний злочин проти природи.
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Pseudoghoul.cfg:17
msgid "Either due to lack of knowledge or on purpose, dark adepts sometimes stop the process of turning a person into a ghoul at an intermediate stage, when the person is still alive, feels everything that happens to them, but ceases to be themselves, although does'nt yet resemble a bloated, disgusting monster. Such creatures are called pseudoghouls - they look like a walking corpse, but their mutated mouths constantly flow with small streams of green acid, which they can spit to poison enemies of their necromancer who committed such a heinous crime against nature."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Pseudoghoul.cfg:22
msgid "infected touch"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Pseudoghoul.cfg:34
msgid "acid spit"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Reaper, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Reaper.cfg:4
msgid "Wesfolk Reaper"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Reaper, race=human
#. Деякі з тих, хто мали б стати чудовими західняцькими воїнами, натомість йдуть схожим проте іншим шляхом — отримавши обладунки з запасів свого Ліч-Лорда, замість бойового топора вони обирають своєю зброєю велику та неймовірно гостру косу, якою вони нещадно проливають кров в ім'я Темряви.
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Reaper.cfg:17
msgid "Some of those who should have become great Wesfolk Warriors instead follow a similar but different path - having received armor from their Lich-Lord's stocks, instead of a battle axe they choose a large and incredibly sharp scythe as their weapon, with which they mercilessly shed blood in the name of Darkness."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=blade
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Reaper.cfg:22
msgid "scythe"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Barrow Wight, race=undead
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Undead_Horse_Barrow_Wight.cfg:4
msgid "Barrow Wight"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Barrow Wight, race=undead
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Undead_Horse_Barrow_Wight.cfg:18
msgid "Perpetually haunted by the fading memory of its former life, a Barrow Wight wanders aimlessly in a delirium of darkness and despair. Their chill essence is shrouded behind cloak and bone, shielding them from most magic."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Pyre Wight, race=undead
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Undead_Horse_Pyre_Wight.cfg:4
msgid "Pyre Wight"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Pyre Wight, race=undead
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Undead_Horse_Pyre_Wight.cfg:18
msgid "Risen from a funeral’s ashes and newly bathed in fire, a Pyre Wight’s soul burns with a desire for vengeance. They single-mindedly seek out those who wronged them in their past life, but undeath has robbed their memories of friend and foe."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Warrior, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Warrior.cfg:4
msgid "Wesfolk Warrior"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Warrior, race=human
#. Отримавши багато бойового досвіду, найкращі з західняцьких бійців отримують від свого Владики кращі обладунки та змінюють свою булаву з шипами на великий дворучний бойовий топор, який набагато легше рубати плоть поки що живих істот во славу Темряви.
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Warrior.cfg:18
msgid "Having gained much combat experience, the best of the Wesfolk Fighters receive better armor from their Lich-Lord and exchange their spiked mace for a large two-handed battle axe, which is much easier to cut the flesh of still living creatures for the glory of Darkness."
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Chariot, gender=male,female, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Chariot.cfg:6
msgid "Wesfolk Chariot"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Chariot, gender=male,female, race=human
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Chariot.cfg:29
msgid "Among the Wesfolk, there are still craftsmen capable of creating a true battle chariot. It is a much more skillful war machine, and its appearance is reminiscent of the heyday of Wesfolk culture. Such chariots were used by the Wesfolk to conquer the plains of the Old Continent in ancient times. Now they are ridden by the senior outlaws. At high speed, in the thick of battle, the blood of their glorious warrior ancestors boils in them, and urges them to fight as bravely and fiercely."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=impact
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Chariot.cfg:50
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Essedum.cfg:54
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Wagon.cfg:43
msgid "trample"
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Chariot.cfg:63
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Wagon.cfg:56
msgid "javelin"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Essedum, race=human , gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Essedum.cfg:6
msgid "Wesfolk Essedum"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Essedum, race=human , gender=male,female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Essedum.cfg:30
msgid "The Essedums are the finest Wesfolk chariots on which their kings and heroes fought in the old days. Now there are only a few Essedums left in the ranks of the Wesfolk. But their riders are armed with the finest Wesfolk weapons and armor, and are determined to remind their enemies of the old days, when the sight of an Essedum charging into battle at full gallop inspired awe."
msgstr ""

#. [attack]: type=pierce
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Essedum.cfg:67
msgid "spear"
msgstr ""

#. [female]: gender=female
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Essedum.cfg:111
msgid "female^Wesfolk Essedum"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Wagon, gender=male,female, race=human 
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Wagon.cfg:6
msgid "Wesfolk Wagon"
msgstr ""

#. [unit_type]: id=Wesfolk Wagon, gender=male,female, race=human 
#: Chasing_the_Light/units/Wesfolk/Wesfolk_Wagon.cfg:29
msgid "The Wesfolk have long been averse to cavalry, instead preferring to charge into the thick of battle on impressive war chariots. Even now, in times of decline, Wesfolk gangs continue to equip war wagons that remotely resemble the chariots of their ancestors. Their ramming combined with a hail of darts is still a formidable force."
msgstr ""

#. [illuminates]: id=illumination, description=
#: Chasing_the_Light/utils/abilities.cfg:13
msgid "illuminates"
msgstr ""

#. [illuminates]: id=illumination, description=
#: Chasing_the_Light/utils/abilities.cfg:14
msgid "female^illuminates"
msgstr ""

